WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:06.595
Every ride you finish now earns XP, worked out by the backend.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.082
Hold your power within ten percent of the target, in a race or a class, and those

00:00:15.082 --> 00:00:17.966
seconds count. The share goes with the ride.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.955
Back comes the XP, line by line: a hundred for finishing, twenty for each rider you

00:00:25.955 --> 00:00:30.029
beat, seventy-five for the podium, and your time on target.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.963
Second of ten against bots, eighty-four percent on target: four hundred and two.

00:00:35.963 --> 00:00:40.195
When streaks arrive, a four-day streak makes it four forty-two.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.318
A solo race or a class has no place to win. A ride that doesn't finish earns

00:00:46.318 --> 00:00:49.988
nothing. And sending a ride twice never pays twice.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.377
What the tests prove: every line of the rule, through the API and in the calculator,

00:00:56.377 --> 00:00:58.546
and the share sent from the ride.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.545
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:06.891 --> 00:01:11.402
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:11.402 --> 00:01:13.073
every hill and interval.

00:01:13.419 --> 00:01:18.597
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:18.597 --> 00:01:24.045
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:24.045 --> 00:01:27.035
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.872
A custom workout lives under Profile.
